    "start": 0.0,
    "end": 5.6,
    "text": "Habitual vitamin D use was associated with a 34% lower risk of contracting COVID-19."
   },
   {
    "id": "t2",
    "start": 5.6,
    "end": 10.96,
    "text": "This was independent of lifestyle, socioeconomic status, or the presence of other chronic diseases."
   },
   {
    "id": "t3",
    "start": 10.96,
    "end": 14.96,
    "text": "The data was also adjusted for other supplement use, like other vitamins and minerals and"
   },
   {
    "id": "t4",
    "start": 14.96,
    "end": 17.6,
    "text": "multivitamins, and there was no association found."
   },
   {
    "id": "t5",
    "start": 17.6,
    "end": 22.8,
    "text": "The best hope we may have in proving whether or not vitamin D has a clinical benefit in COVID-19"
   },
   {
    "id": "t6",
    "start": 22.8,
    "end": 27.2,
    "text": "may be in large population studies where vitamin D is taken prophylactically."
   }
  ]
 },
